From 8ffbc4717500c86622779ecd634948b32a6e6f5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 94/94] consensus: open the P2MR rescue lane on Ark-0 at height
 51000

H4R, the height from which the Ark-0 signet opens the rescue lane, is
decided: 51000, the height at the release plus two weeks of blocks,
rounded up to the thousand, about two weeks after the release. It is
fixed in the code as ARK0_RESCUE_HEIGHT, as 32000 was for
OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S; the lane relaxes the rules (a hard fork), the height
is announced at least two weeks before it, and it never changes once a
build carrying it has been announced. A first build of this patch, with
63000 and four weeks, was published on 2026-10-30 and replaced the same
day, before it was announced.

ark0_lane_closed becomes ark0_rescue_height: the deployment is enabled
at 51000, and the script flags of Ark-0 blocks at heights 50999 and 51000
differ by exactly SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE; the default signet, the
testnets and mainnet still never open the lane. doc/p2mr-rescue.md says
Ark-0 opens the lane from block 51000, what an operator of a node
without the lane must know, and that the single-check gate decides on
its paused runs, with the continuous maxima of both machines.
