-**The hard fork.** A node without this build (an M3 or M4-S node) finds the first block with a rescue
-spend invalid, marks it so, and stops: on a network whose blocks one party signs, it has no other
-chain to follow, as long as that party extends only one chain. Upgraded later, it still has the block
-marked invalid: `bitcoin-cli reconsiderblock <hash of that block>` lets it continue.
+**The hard fork: what an operator must know.** A node without the lane (an M3 or M4-S build) refuses
+the first block with a rescue spend, marks it invalid, and stops following the chain there: on a
+network whose blocks one party signs, it has no other chain to follow, as long as that party extends
+only one chain. Once upgraded, it still has the block marked invalid, and continues after
+`bitcoin-cli reconsiderblock <hash of that block>`, as `feature_p2mr_rescue.py` shows. On Ark-0 that
+block can come from height 51000 on.
 
